…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚ$And it was so on the morrow, that Saul put the people in three companies; and they came into the midst of the host in the morning watch, and slew the Ammonites until the heat of the day: and it came to pass, that they which remained were scattered, so that two of them were not left together.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ}And the people said unto Samuel, Who is he that said, Shall Saul reign over us? bring the men, that we may put them to death.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtAnd Saul said, There shall not a man be put to death this day: for to day the LORD hath wrought salvation in Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ[Then said Samuel to the people, Come, and let us go to Gilgal, and renew the kingdom there.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙßAnd all the people went to Gilgal; and there they made Saul king before the LORD in Gilgal; and there they sacrificed sacrifices of peace offerings before the LORD; and there Saul and all the men of Israel rejoiced greatly.¦layout ªlast_verse